==Old English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{recons|ehwaz||horse|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{recons|h₁éḱwos||horse|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with {{osx}} {{l|osx|ehuskalk|''ehu''skalk|lang=osx}} "horse-rider", Old High German [[eha-]] (in personal names), Old Norse ''[[jór]]''.  The Indo-European root is also the source of Latin ''[[equus]]'', Avestan ''aspa-'', Sanskrit {{term|अश्व|sc=Deva|tr=áśva|lang=sa}}, Old Armenian {{term|էշ||donkey|tr=ēš|lang=xcl}}, Tocharian A ''[[yuk]]'' B ''[[yakwe]]'', Proto-Baltic {{recons|ečwā-|lang=bat-pro}} (Lithuanian ''[[ašva|ašvà]]''), Old Irish ''[[ech]]'' (Irish ''[[each]]'').

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/eoh/|[eox]|lang=ang}}

====Noun====
{{head|ang|noun|g=m|g2=n}}

# {{poetic|lang=ang}} [[horse]], [[steed]]

